  "title": "A Bird’s-Eye View: SLS Core Stage at Stennis",
  "description": "NASA and contractor teams conducted Green Run testing of the first Space Launch System core stage on the B-2 Test Stand at Stennis Space Center, culminating with a final hot fire test of the stage and its four RS-25 engines in March 2021. The accompanying video features drone footage of various Green Run activities at Stennis, including the arrival, installation, testing, removal, loading , and departure of the core stage from the south Mississippi site.",
